    "reviewChecks": [
      "Exact5-file combined patch reviewed; three original production owners only, no public capability/interface/exports/dependency change.",
      "Original timer point and numeric duration preserved via one Date.now sample. Request cutoff equals earlier of existing context deadline and the original30000ms timer. Control still starts before request-body consumption.",
      "Admission joins only its original tracked promise after signal abort and before original cutoff. Successful settlement still rethrows original cancellation; downstream credential/fetch rechecks and finally release remain.",
      "Ordinary joined rejection may be sanitized only after observed original callback settlement. Typed UNKNOWN, cleanup_unknown code, release failure, pending or at-cutoff outcome stays uncertain. Late original work remains tracked and releases once.",
      "Original native-cut, bounded await, driver latch, body cleanup and dispose limits are unchanged. The late-admission HTTP scenario retains UNKNOWN after its original cut failure even after release and repeated dispose.",
      "The existing HTTP sibling scenario keeps its original five requests and ordinary-failure oracle. New controlled cases retain exact admissions/credentials/HTTP/release counts, actual callback abort and fixed original cutoff; no failed native read is turned into success.",
      "All final source and six protected hashes match frozen manifest. Source R2 does not substitute for the final original full check still in progress."
    ],
    "executionGate": "Final original pnpm check with retained exact packed-consumer archives is required before publication. Original resulting-head CI and app/native acceptance remain separate."
